  "body": "## Background\r\n\r\nCurrently, the spec [defines](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#valid-browsing-context-name-or-keyword) `_blank`, `_self`, `_parent`, or `_top` as valid browsing context keywords.\r\n\r\nIn the context of [installed PWAs](https://web.dev/progressive-web-apps/#installable) (or *web applications added to the home screen* on iOS), all [out-of-scope](https://w3c.github.io/manifest/#navigation-scope) off-origin links traditionally open in an in-app browser. This can be verified by installing this [test app](https://piotrswigon.github.io/pwa-demo/standalone/) and trying the off-origin examples. This is true for Android, iOS, and desktop (note the UI of the in-app browser at the top of each screenshot):\r\n\r\n- **Android:**\r\n  <img width=\"200\" alt=\"Android\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/145676/98804104-05caf680-2416-11eb-95f5-6846dffd29c3.png\">\r\n- **iOS:** \r\n  <img width=\"200\" alt=\"iOS\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/145676/98804122-0e233180-2416-11eb-969e-f1b2248567d8.png\">\r\n- **macOS:**\r\n  <img width=\"200\" alt=\"macOS\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/145676/98804143-167b6c80-2416-11eb-864b-d6b78298fc8a.png\">\r\n\r\n## The Problem\r\n\r\nThere is currently no way for developers to create links that break *out* of the context of the PWA and just open in the user's default browser ([more context](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=709889)). \r\n\r\n## Proposal\r\n\r\nWhat are people's thoughts around specifying another browsing context keyword tentatively called `_browser` that would in the general case when running in a browser behave like `_blank`, but in the context of an installed PWA would open in a new browser tab (or window if no window exists), defaulting to a relationship to the current PWA of `rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"`?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
